Subject: [PATCH] psa: initialize the complete MAC driver context

PSA_MAC_OPERATION_INIT initializes the first unsigned member of a union.
Its remaining storage can retain unspecified bytes, including the nested
HMAC hash operation id. Initialize the driver context before dispatch, as
psa_hash_setup already does, while retaining active-operation rejection.

diff --git a/library/psa_crypto.c b/library/psa_crypto.c
index 82e28dcb1..828586e1d 100644
--- a/library/psa_crypto.c
+++ b/library/psa_crypto.c
@@ -2476,6 +2476,11 @@ static psa_status_t psa_mac_setup(psa_mac_operation_t *operation,
         goto exit;
     }
 
+    /* PSA_MAC_OPERATION_INIT only directly zeroes the int-sized dummy member
+     * of the driver context union. Initialize the whole context before a
+     * driver accesses its nested operations, such as the hash used by HMAC. */
+    memset(&operation->ctx, 0, sizeof(operation->ctx));
+
     operation->is_sign = is_sign;
     /* Dispatch the MAC setup call with validated input */
     if (is_sign) {
